From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bas=20Magr=C3=A9?= <bas@opvolger.net>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:07:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] drm/amdgpu: Map GTT write-combined on non-coherent
 devices
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On platforms where PCIe DMA does not snoop the CPU caches (e.g. the
SpacemiT K1, "dma-noncoherent"), a cached GTT buffer is broken: CPU
writes such as ring buffer commands stay in the CPU cache and the GPU
reads stale RAM, so the ring test times out:

  amdgpu: ring gfx test failed (-110)

Map all GTT buffers write-combined on such devices.  The SpacemiT
vendor kernel does the same under CONFIG_SOC_SPACEMIT_K1X.

Signed-off-by: Bas Magré <bas@opvolger.net>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
index 83968886c29a..783f3a8a7134 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
+#include <linux/dma-map-ops.h>
 #include <linux/iommu.h>
 #include <linux/pagemap.h>
 #include <linux/sched/task.h>
@@ -1213,6 +1214,17 @@ static struct ttm_tt *amdgpu_ttm_tt_create(struct ttm_buffer_object *bo,
 	else
 		caching = ttm_cached;
 
+	/*
+	 * On platforms where PCIe DMA does not snoop the CPU caches (e.g. the
+	 * SpacemiT K1, "dma-noncoherent"), a cached GTT buffer is broken: CPU
+	 * writes (ring buffer commands) stay in the CPU cache and the GPU reads
+	 * stale RAM, so the ring test times out.  Map all GTT buffers
+	 * write-combined (uncached) on such devices.  The SpacemiT vendor kernel
+	 * does the same with an #ifdef CONFIG_SOC_SPACEMIT_K1X.
+	 */
+	if (!dev_is_dma_coherent(adev->dev))
+		caching = ttm_write_combined;
+
 	/* allocate space for the uninitialized page entries */
 	if (ttm_sg_tt_init(&gtt->ttm, bo, page_flags, caching)) {
 		kfree(gtt);
